  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% acc, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) is only 20.8%, confirming RNA is the dominant modality. The current best RNA encoder is a simple linear PCA (2000 dims). Uncertainty: We have no evidence yet about whether a powerful learned RNA encoder (scgpt, a pretrained single-cell transformer) can extract substantially more signal than PCA. This experiment (config_007: rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, isolating the RNA encoder choice. If scgpt significantly outperforms PCA, it validates investing in learned encoders and justifies exploring them in multimodal settings. If it does not, it indicates the RNA signal is already well-captured by linear structure, redirecting effort toward profile settings or fusion. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-impact, high-uncertainty question before testing multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion avoids confounding multiple design changes in a single experiment."
}

